\title{[GCD4] Fibonacci number size (3 pts)}
\date{2026-09-01T17:45:20Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{problem}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{How big are [Fibonacci numbers](00BL)? Let’s find out:

\ol{
  \li{Solve #{x^2 = x + 1} for #{x} and call the positive solution #{\varphi} (this is often known as the \em{golden ratio}) and the negative solution #{\hat{\varphi}}.}
  \li{Explain why we know that #{\varphi^2 = \varphi + 1} and #{\hat{\varphi}^2 = \hat{\varphi} + 1}.
  \hint{Your answer should be one sentence!}
  }
  \li{Show that #{\varphi^{k+2} = \varphi^{k+1}
    + \varphi^k} for all #{k \geq 0} (by starting with #{\varphi^2 =
    \varphi + 1} and multiplying both sides by #{\varphi^k}). Note that the same is also true with #{\hat{\varphi}} in place of #{\varphi}.}
  \li{Now prove by induction on #{n} that #{F_n = \frac{1}{\sqrt 5}(\varphi^n -
  \hat{\varphi}^n)}.
  \hint{Don’t forget that you need two base cases; you will want to show that #{\varphi - \hat{\varphi} = \sqrt 5}.}
  }
  \li{
    Conclude that #{F_n \approx \varphi^n/\sqrt 5}.
    \hint{What can you say about #{\hat{\varphi}^n} as #{n} gets large?}
  }
}

}
